        "q": "What is the hardest part of building a running app?",
        "a": "Reliable background GPS tracking. Both iOS and Android deliberately restrict background location to protect battery and privacy, so you must work within their rules: iOS needs Always authorization and a background mode, and Android needs a foreground service with a persistent notification plus separate background-location permission. On top of that, raw GPS is noisy and needs smoothing, and continuous high-accuracy tracking drains the battery, so there is a real accuracy-versus-battery trade-off to make deliberately."
