        "q": "Should cycle data stay on the device or sync to a server?",
        "a": "On-device-only is a legitimate architecture here, unlike in most health apps, because the dataset is small, single-user and useful without a server. It is also a hard product constraint: no cross-device sync, no web app, no account recovery, no server-side analysis and no support engineer able to inspect a broken record. The alternative is end-to-end encrypted sync, which trades those back for a key-management problem, since losing the last device can mean losing the data. Decide before you build, because reversing it later is a rewrite."
