        "q": "Should a cycling app record rides itself or just import them?",
        "a": "Pick one for version one. Recording live means owning a multi-sensor Bluetooth session that survives dropouts for hours, plus battery and background work. Importing means your product is analysis and your engineering goes into deduplication and normalisation across sources. Serious riders often already record on a head unit, so the importer path reaches them without asking them to change anything, while the recorder path reaches riders who only carry a phone. Building both before either works well is the most common way this category stalls."
