        "a": "Offline maps are the paid feature, because they are the thing that only matters when you cannot get it another way. Usage is episodic, so annual pricing is the only shape that works: someone who hikes four times a year will not carry a monthly subscription between trips. Regional or one-off map packs convert travellers who will never subscribe. Clubs, guides and land managers are realistic institutional buyers. The main renewal risk is being forgotten between trips rather than being disliked."
