        "q": "What do I need to consider before building a fitness app for children?",
        "a": "Settle the constraints before the features. Decide your audience age range, your markets, exactly what data each planned feature requires, who consents to it and how that consent is recorded and revoked. Then design the schema around the smallest record that makes each feature work. Doing this in the other order means rebuilding, because a data flow that looked harmless in a design review can be the reason the app cannot ship. Which specific obligations apply to your app is a question for qualified counsel."
